{"task_id": "HumanEval/27", "solution": "```python\ndef flip_case(string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" For a given string, flip lowercase characters to uppercase and uppercase to lowercase.\n    >>> flip_case('Hello')\n    'hELLO'\n    \"\"\"\n    flipped_chars = []\n    for char in string:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':  # Check if character is a lowercase letter\n            flipped_chars.append(chr(ord(char) - 32))  # Convert to uppercase\n        elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':  # Check if character is an uppercase letter\n            flipped_chars.append(chr(ord(char) + 32))  # Convert to lowercase\n        else:\n            flipped_chars.append(char)  # Keep non-alphabetic characters as they are\n    return \"\".join(flipped_chars)\n```"}
