{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_even(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the odd indicies, while its values at the even indicies are equal\n    to the values of the even indicies of l, but sorted.\n    >>> sort_even([1, 2, 3])\n    [1, 2, 3]\n    >>> sort_even([5, 6, 3, 4])\n    [3, 6, 5, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        return []\n\n    # Create a copy of the input list for the output (l').\n    # This preserves odd-indexed elements by default.\n    l_prime = l[:]\n\n    # Extract elements from even indices into a temporary list.\n    even_elements = []\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            even_elements.append(l[i])\n\n    # Sort the temporary list of even-indexed elements.\n    even_elements.sort()\n\n    # Iterate through l' and replace elements at even indices with sorted elements from the temporary list.\n    even_idx_ptr = 0\n    for i in range(len(l_prime)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            l_prime[i] = even_elements[even_idx_ptr]\n            even_idx_ptr += 1\n\n    return l_prime\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_cyclic(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    takes as input string encoded with encode_cyclic function. Returns decoded string.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_groups = []\n    for i in range(0, len(s), 3):\n        group = s[i : i + 3]\n        if len(group) == 3:\n            # If the group is c2c3c1, decode to c1c2c3\n            decoded_groups.append(group[2] + group[0] + group[1])\n        else:\n            decoded_groups.append(group)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_groups)\n```"}
