{"task_id": "HumanEval/39", "solution": "```python\ndef prime_fib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    prime_fib returns n-th number that is a Fibonacci number and it's also prime.\n    >>> prime_fib(1)\n    2\n    >>> prime_fib(2)\n    3\n    >>> prime_fib(3)\n    5\n    >>> prime_fib(4)\n    13\n    >>> prime_fib(5)\n    89\n    \"\"\"\n    from typing import Iterator\n\n    def _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        _is_prime checks if a number is prime.\n        A prime number is a natural number greater than 1.\n        \"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        for i in range(2, int(num**0.5) + 1):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def _fibonacci_generator() -> Iterator[int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        _fibonacci_generator yields an infinite sequence of Fibonacci numbers.\n        The sequence starts with 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, ...\n        \"\"\"\n        a, b = 1, 1\n        while True:\n            yield a\n            a, b = b, a + b\n\n    prime_fib_count = 0\n    fib_gen = _fibonacci_generator()\n\n    result = 0\n    for current_fib_num in fib_gen:\n        if _is_prime(current_fib_num):\n            prime_fib_count += 1\n            if prime_fib_count == n:\n                result = current_fib_num\n                break\n    return result\n```"}
