{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # Odd number of elements, return the middle element\n        return float(sorted_l[n // 2])\n    else:\n        # Even number of elements, return the average of the two middle elements\n        return (sorted_l[n // 2 - 1] + sorted_l[n // 2]) / 2.0"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence using an iterative approach.\n    Handles base cases for n=0, 1, 2, 3 and then iteratively calculates subsequent values.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the sequence with the first four values\n    sequence_values = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    # Iterate from the 4th element up to n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib4 = (\n            sequence_values[i - 1]\n            + sequence_values[i - 2]\n            + sequence_values[i - 3]\n            + sequence_values[i - 4]\n        )\n        sequence_values.append(next_fib4)\n\n    return sequence_values[n]\n```"}
