{"task_id": "HumanEval/80", "solution": "```python\ndef is_happy(s):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a string is happy: has length at least 3 and every 3 consecutive letters are distinct.\n    Returns True if happy, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(s) < 3:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(len(s) - 2):\n        # Extract a 3-character sequence\n        char1 = s[i]\n        char2 = s[i+1]\n        char3 = s[i+2]\n\n        # Check if the three characters are distinct\n        if char1 == char2 or char1 == char3 or char2 == char3:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/76", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef is_simple_power(x, n):\n    \"\"\"Checks if x is a simple power of n, i.e., n**i = x for a non-negative integer i.\"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return x == 1\n    elif n == 0:\n        return x == 0 or x == 1\n\n    if n < 0:\n        return x == 1 # Only n^0 = 1 is a simple power for non-negative integer exponents.\n\n    if x <= 0:\n        return False # For positive n, n^i (i>=0) cannot be zero or negative, except 0^0=1, 0^i=0 handled above.\n\n    try:\n        # Calculate the logarithm to find the potential exponent 'i'.\n        exponent = math.log(x, n)\n        # Check if the exponent is a non-negative integer using float comparison.\n        return exponent >= 0 and math.isclose(exponent, round(exponent))\n    except (ValueError, ZeroDivisionError):\n        # Handles cases like log(negative, base), log(x, 1) if not caught earlier, or log(x, 0).\n        return False\n```\n"}
